Image 1 is a photo of a door or window. Image 2 is a line drawing of the one we built from it: {built}
Compare them. Count the leaves that open or slide, the panes of the transom (the row above the first horizontal bar), which leaves have a handle or pull, and which sliding leaves are on the front rail (their edge covers the next leaf). Leaves are numbered from 0, left to right as seen in the photo.
Answer with ONE JSON object only: {"same": true|false, "corrections": {only what differs, any of "style" (swing, sliding, folding, fixed, top-hung), "leaves", "transomPanes", "handles": [leaf numbers], "fronts": [leaf numbers], "axesRatio": [vertical dividers as fractions of the width from the left], "hAxesRatio": [horizontal dividers as fractions of the height from the sill]}, "notes": [short reasons]}. Sizes are not compared: the drawing keeps the size of the hole. If they match, answer {"same": true, "corrections": {}}.
